// Captain Sable, cormorant, the Ferrymen (bible 3.5). The Drowned Quay, room A.
// Voice (style guide 4): clipped; ends conversations first; names the price of everything; never "I hope".
// Her image: prices. Cryptic register (style guide 6): withhold, never lie.
// She met Wren on the shore (Prologue_Shore_Wake sets saltmarrow.met_sable). This file is every talk after.
// State she reads: saltmarrow.sable.*, the Reedmother vantage, the Bone Bridge and Tether-Widows commissions,
// the quay's fate, Merrow's End erased, the Lamp-Keeper, Halvard (act1.unlicensed), the walk.

title: Quay_Sable
---
<<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.talked")>>
    <<jump Quay_Sable_First>>
<<endif>>
<<jump Quay_Sable_Again>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_First
---
Sable: Found your feet, then. The boardwalk charges by the plank. #line:04ec1af
Sable: Word came up the coast before you did. The Guild's declared Isolde Marr dead. #plant:5.2 #line:0db64fa
Sable: And a journeyman missing. Same day. They were quick about it. #plant:5.2 #line:0fe970e
-> Quick isn't the same as sure. #line:0ce18a2
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Sable: No. But it's cheaper. #line:0bd4754
-> She isn't dead. #line:0de39ab
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Nobody comes out. That's the price of going in. I don't set it. #line:03aadda
-> ... #line:020eb6d
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Quiet costs nothing. Keep it. #line:043c8aa
Sable: You'll want the desk, the board, and the lamp up the chain. In that order. #line:04c5f18
Sable: The lamp's not free either. Nothing that still remembers is. #plant:5.6 #line:0fdcd96
<<flag saltmarrow.sable.talked 1>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_Again
---
<<if place_fate("Saltmarrow_A") == "anchored">>
    Sable: Anchored, then. The same tide every day now. You'll get used to it. Everyone does. #still #line:07a13bc
    Sable: The Wardens don't buy anything. Bad for trade. #still #line:009c3fe
<<elseif place_fate("Saltmarrow_A") == "held">>
    Sable: Held, is it. Roll-call at dusk. Don't be late; a bird nobody names is a bird nobody keeps. #still #line:0f459b3
<<elseif place_fate("Saltmarrow_A") == "released">>
    Sable: You let it go. Honest, at least. I'll sell tethers while there's a post to tie them to. #still #line:0e9e3d0
<<elseif has_flag("act1.unlicensed")>>
    Sable: Unlicensed. He said it loud enough for the reeds. #still #line:09fc3ee
    Sable: Prices are the same. That's the one thing the Guild can't fix. #still #line:0e606c9
<<elseif has_flag("boss.lamp_keeper.defeated")>>
    Sable: Fourth light's up. Ships will see it. So will the Guild. #still #line:02eba6b
<<else>>
    Sable: Still here. Still lost. Both cost the same. #still #line:0695736
<<endif>>
<<if erased("Saltmarrow_B")>>
    Sable: Bells in the reeds. Merrow's End went off your page, didn't it. #still #line:05adab6
    Sable: Draw it again. That's what the quill is for. The bell doesn't charge; the walk back does. #still #line:0378ecf
<<endif>>
<<if commission_is("saltmarrow.tether_widows", "taken") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.widow.decided")>>
    <<jump Quay_Sable_Widow>>
<<elseif has_flag("saltmarrow.widow.met") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.widow_heard")>>
    <<jump Quay_Sable_Widow_Met>>
<<endif>>
<<if surveyed("Saltmarrow_A/Reedmother")>>
    <<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.reed")>>
        Sable: You drew the Reedmother. Hm. Guild after all, or good at pretending. #line:0723e53
        <<flag saltmarrow.sable.reed 1>>
    <<endif>>
    <<if commission_is("saltmarrow.bone_bridge", "taken") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.bone_bridge.heard")>>
        Sable: Whale sang while you were up there. Under the bridge. You hear it? #still #line:02c3db4
        -> I heard it. It sounded like names. #line:0e2e1fb
            <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
            Sable: Everyone says names. Nobody agrees whose. #plant:3.4 #line:03b9cd0
            <<flag saltmarrow.bone_bridge.heard 1>>
        -> I heard nothing. #line:0ff71b0
            <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
            Sable: Then you weren't listening. Go again. It's bones; it'll wait. #still #line:0a39711
        -> ... #line:02316e4
            <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
            Sable: That's how it starts. Listening for it. #still #line:08823bd
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Sable: There's a vantage by the old reed. Draw it, if the cowl's honest. #still #line:01c329f
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.ledger")>>
    Sable: Board by the desk is the ledger. People write what they want and can't say aloud. #line:0b6a494
    Sable: Read that far down, if you like. Nobody else does. #line:0a71fa2
    <<flag saltmarrow.sable.ledger 1>>
<<endif>>
<<if walked("Saltmarrow_B")>>
    <<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.walked")>>
        Sable: Heard you walked the old woman's bounds. Nobody sells that. I checked. #line:0fbe33c
        <<flag saltmarrow.sable.walked 1>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("act2.started") and not has_flag("sable.windreach_offered")>>
    Sable: Steppe's open, they say. South road, through Lowmarket. Long way round. #line:0c26532
    Sable: Ferrymen used to row there. Up the Dry River, when it was wet. Sea still is. #line:0cbed34
    <<flag sable.windreach_offered 1>>
<<endif>>
-> What are you selling? #line:082f994
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Tools. Ferrymen's prices. #still #line:0457a7c
    <<if has_flag("saltmarrow.iris_burned")>>
        Sable: Dearer than they were. Ask the ones who burned the fields. #still #line:0b3f86f
    <<endif>>
    <<if has_flag("sable.windreach_offered") and flag("sable.boat_at") != 2>>
        Sable: And the boat north. That one's not for sale. It's free. #still #line:09780c1
        -> The tools. #line:0bdb2d5
            <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
            <<shop Saltmarrow>>
        -> The boat north. To the steppe. #line:063543c
            <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
            <<if not has_flag("sable.windreach_rowed")>>
                Sable: No price. I want to see if they're still there. Get in. #line:00c268d
            <<else>>
                Sable: Same boat. Same water. Get in. #line:02799ba
            <<endif>>
            <<row windreach>>
    <<else>>
        <<shop Saltmarrow>>
    <<endif>>
-> The third lighthouse. Who keeps it? <<if has_flag("boss.lamp_keeper.defeated") and not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.aury")>> #line:02f3a83
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Nobody. It faded. There's a tether to it on the post; price on the tag. #line:04e2f6a
    Sable: My brother kept it. Keeps it. He doesn't know the difference. #plant:4.1 #line:0b53921
    Sable: Don't tell him. That's not a price. That's a favour. #line:03f72ab
    <<flag saltmarrow.sable.aury 1>>
-> Nothing today. #line:0b72e2a
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Cheaper. #still #line:0d7eb7a
===

title: Quay_Sable_Widow
---
Sable: The widow at the tether-post asked after you. First time she's asked after anyone. #line:0e14292
Sable: She means to go in after him. Rope's already round her waist. I sold it to her. #line:02a58b5
-> Talk her out of it. #line:011c394
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Sable: I'll carry it. She won't listen. They never do, and then they do. #line:0bcf3ef
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 1>>
-> Then somebody goes with her. Me. #line:00b4603
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Then I hold the other end. I've held worse. #line:0d72818
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 2>>
-> ... #line:0a60e5e
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Sable: That's an answer too. She'll take it as the second one. #line:0c8179b
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 2>>
<<jump Quay_Sable_Count>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_Widow_Met
---
// She was answered at the post herself (Tether_Knot); Sable heard, and gives the count all the same.
Sable: You went to the post yourself. Nobody does that. They send me. #line:0857deb
<<if flag("saltmarrow.widow.decided") == 1>>
    Sable: She gave Skua his rope back. He didn't know what to charge. #line:0e4a225
<<else>>
    Sable: I held the other end. Forty paces, and the tide. I'm not saying what came up the rope. #line:070fb02
<<endif>>
<<jump Quay_Sable_Count>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_Count
---
// The number she gives away, once, after the widow is answered either way: her bound memory (flavour-text.md).
Sable: You'll want something true for that page of yours. Here. It's free. #line:0032910
Sable: Since the fall, eleven hundred and six boats have come back to this quay. I counted every one. #line:02cea24
Sable: That's the number I give away. #line:07698e0
<<flag saltmarrow.sable.widow_heard 1>>
<<bind sable.boats_back>>
===

title: Quay_Sable_Night
---
// Night post: asleep under the stilts. The same every night; in an anchored quay, every loop.
Sable: Quay's shut. So am I. #still #line:01df1f3
Sable: Morning, if you're still here. Most aren't. #still #line:0f8e732
===
